.TH lwoodz-cli 1  "lwoodz-cli 0.2.0"
.SH NAME
lwoodz\-cli \- CLI companion for the lwoodz licensing daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlwoodz\-cli\fR [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
CLI companion for the lwoodz licensing daemon
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<PATH>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output as JSON (must come before the subcommand, e.g. `lwoodz\-cli \-\-json audit`)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
lwoodz\-cli\-init(1)
Create lwoodz.toml in the current directory
.TP
lwoodz\-cli\-generate(1)
Generate LICENSE and related legal documents
.TP
lwoodz\-cli\-audit(1)
Run a full compliance audit
.TP
lwoodz\-cli\-check(1)
Check dependency license compatibility only
.TP
lwoodz\-cli\-licenses(1)
List known SPDX license identifiers
.TP
lwoodz\-cli\-compat(1)
Check whether two SPDX identifiers are compatible
.TP
lwoodz\-cli\-detect(1)
Detect the SPDX license of a LICENSE file
.TP
lwoodz\-cli\-explain(1)
Explain an SPDX license (uses Groq if GROQ_API_KEY is set)
.TP
lwoodz\-cli\-headers(1)
Insert/update copyright + SPDX headers in source files
.TP
lwoodz\-cli\-dual(1)
Generate a dual\-licensed variant
.TP
lwoodz\-cli\-status(1)
Show daemon and repository status
.TP
lwoodz\-cli\-version(1)
Print the version
.TP
lwoodz\-cli\-completions(1)
Print a shell completion script to stdout
.TP
lwoodz\-cli\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.2.0
